1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
= kisskh.asia =

2
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:45,159
Fu Ming Yu's actually got something.

3
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,200
I never thought my work
would be presented like this.

4
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:53,238
Wait, you're impressed with him again?

5
00:01:53,239 --> 00:01:54,839
Not at all.

6
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,799
The way he disrespected me as a creator?

7
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,439
I'm not letting that go.

8
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,718
Good.

9
00:02:00,719 --> 00:02:03,078
He's not that talented or capable.

10
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:06,122
I'm telling you,
the only reason he's working so hard

11
00:02:06,123 --> 00:02:08,515
is that he's got his eye on that female pilot.

12
00:02:08,516 --> 00:02:10,839
Which one? There are three of them.

13
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,999
The young one, obviously.

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,959
He might as well have

15
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:17,478
"I like Ruan Si Xian"
written across his forehead.

16
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:20,200
He's trying to steal my girl.

17
00:02:21,623 --> 00:02:23,039
He likes Ruan Si Xian?

18
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,040
Of course!

19
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,119
Otherwise, I'd have already won her over.

20
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:32,599
That morning, I sent over a huge bouquet,

21
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:37,600
but he cut in,
and in the end she never even saw my flowers.

22
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,199
[Chang Xiao Yi]

23
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,879
I have to say,
with your whole playbook on chasing girls,

24
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:50,639
only the one you're ignoring now
would fall for it.

25
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,840
[Chang Xiao Yi]

26
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,878
So, do me a solid?

27
00:03:01,879 --> 00:03:03,079
No.

28
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,559
You made your own mess. You clean it up.

29
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,839
Come on, help me deal with her.

30
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,959
She's driving me crazy.

31
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,198
We broke up,
but she keeps bugging me every single day.

32
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:13,839
If she's bugging you, then call the police.

33
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:16,799
What's the point of sitting here
complaining to me?

34
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,999
That's not really cool, is it?

35
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,479
We did truly love each other.

36
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:22,758
Taking it to court would be a mess.

37
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:24,919
Just help me out. I want some peace.

38
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:29,918
Never would've guessed
that Mr. Yan is such a sentimental guy.

39
00:03:29,919 --> 00:03:31,119
- Of course.
- Come here.

40
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,439
I'll tell you what to do.

41
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:39,100
Just keep climbing, get on that wall,
and you'll have total peace.

42
00:03:39,102 --> 00:03:40,565
No way. Not again.

43
00:03:40,567 --> 00:03:42,247
Come on.

44
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,399
I can't take it anymore.

45
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:48,160
Don't give me that. Get moving.

46
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,360
[Episode 6]
[A Slight Stirring of the Heart]

47
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,039
What's the plan?

48
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,720
Follow him.

49
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,958
Don't take it off. Cameras everywhere.

50
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:25,078
I'm not wearing it.

51
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:30,080
A mask would make me stand out.

52
00:04:30,759 --> 00:04:33,239
Don't make any moves yet.

53
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:36,319
We need to act,

54
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:37,439
act...

55
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,440
Carefully?

56
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,119
I've got a weird feeling.

57
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,279
He couldn't have remembered something,
could he?

58
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:48,758
Otherwise, why would he carry my suitcase
and set up a meeting with Captain Huang Ying?

59
00:04:48,759 --> 00:04:50,520
Something's definitely up.

60
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,560
Who is it?

61
00:05:03,716 --> 00:05:05,479
Yan An?

62
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,400
What's he doing here so late?

63
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,760
Hi.

64
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,159
Mr. Yan.

65
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,278
What brings you here?

66
00:05:24,279 --> 00:05:25,879
Still calling me Mr. Yan?

67
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,439
We're way past that.

68
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,839
Just call me Yan An.

69
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,438
It's so late.

70
00:05:30,439 --> 00:05:32,279
What are you doing here?

71
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,398
Nothing much.

72
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:36,438
I was on a business trip overseas days ago.
I just got back tonight.

73
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:40,680
Got you something.

74
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,039
Called earlier, but you didn't pick up.

75
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:46,398
I happen to be staying nearby,
so I thought I'd drop it off.

76
00:05:46,399 --> 00:05:48,199
I can't take this.

77
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,039
Why not? It's not expensive.

78
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,959
No, you know, with us--

79
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,159
- What about us?
- I really--

80
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,838
That's exactly why you should take it.
Trust me, you can.

81
00:05:54,839 --> 00:05:56,960
- I really can't.
- Take it.

82
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:03,239
You'll hurt my feelings if you don't take it.

83
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,119
No, seriously, I can't.

84
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,919
Hey!

85
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,919
There, you'll take it now, right?

86
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:12,799
If you feel bad,
just treat me to dinner the day after tomorrow.

87
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,119
I'll take that as a yes.

88
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,199
Get some rest.

89
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,880
Good night.

90
00:06:43,114 --> 00:06:45,479
What are you doing? He's gone.

91
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,759
He didn't even get through the door.

92
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,159
Didn't you hear?

93
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,759
She said yes.

94
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,959
Yan An will definitely be back in a bit.

95
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:57,838
No proof.

96
00:06:57,839 --> 00:06:59,479
Listen to me.

97
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:02,378
Now that we've known this place,

98
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:06,679
we'll wait by the door and wait for him.

99
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,199
Why would I wait with him?

100
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,914
I'm going to get her--

101
00:07:09,916 --> 00:07:11,919
No rush.

102
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,680
Then what's the plan?

103
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:18,580
- Wait.
- Wait for what?

104
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,280
What are your plans for tomorrow?

105
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,600
Busy.

106
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,960
You're off both tomorrow and the day after.

107
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,319
Can't I be busy on my days off?

108
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,919
I'm going running, boxing,

109
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,840
doing practice questions,
and simulator training.

110
00:07:44,356 --> 00:07:46,359
I'm working on my combat skills,

111
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:49,958
so if anyone ever tries to get handsy with me,
I won't even need the police.

112
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,240
I can handle it myself.

113
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:58,679
Ruan Si Xian, I'll say this one last time.

114
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:01,160
I didn't do it on purpose today.

115
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,920
Not on purpose?

116
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,526
Not on purpose?

117
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,959
Hey, wake up.

118
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:31,958
Your snoring
kept the motion-sensor lights on all night.

119
00:08:31,959 --> 00:08:33,278
We can't just sit here.

120
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:34,760
Let's move.

121
00:08:38,639 --> 00:08:40,558
Did he go in?

122
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:42,119
- Can't see.
- Forget it.

123
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:44,199
He's not here. Isn't that mistress there?

124
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,079
Just go--

125
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,319
Relax.

126
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,119
- Let's talk it over.
- Talk about what?

127
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,279
We're already at the door!

128
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:53,639
- Who is it?
- Mr. Yan?

129
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,038
Yan An? Are you in there?

130
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:56,359
Looking for Yan An?

131
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,120
Yan An!

132
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,240
Yan An, are you here?

133
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,039
Yan An isn't here.

134
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,159
Yan An!

135
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,759
We're looking for Yan An.

136
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,159
Yan An?

137
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,638
This is my house.

138
00:09:10,639 --> 00:09:11,959
You two-timer.

139
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,398
What are you doing?

140
00:09:13,399 --> 00:09:15,918
- I'm looking for Yan An.
- Yan An isn't here. This is my house.

141
00:09:15,919 --> 00:09:17,879
Your house?

142
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,519
Yan An bought this for you, didn't he?

143
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:20,638
You don't deserve it.

144
00:09:20,639 --> 00:09:22,839
Cheater and the side piece. Got it on my phone!

145
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:25,199
Yan An! Come out! Yan An!

146
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,799
- What are you doing in my room?
- Yan An!

147
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:27,839
Hiding in bed?

148
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,759
- I'm calling the police!
- Yan An!

149
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,519
I'll use force.

150
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,558
I'm warning you, I'll use force.

151
00:09:32,559 --> 00:09:34,800
- In the closet?
- Are you going to stop?

152
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:38,520
No violence. Be polite.

153
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:42,080
You broke into my house! How dare you say that?

154
00:09:47,726 --> 00:09:49,966
They're trying to hurt me.

155
00:09:56,267 --> 00:09:59,827
You attacked me with a spray bottle!

156
00:10:10,879 --> 00:10:13,200
And you accused me of breaking into your house?

157
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,599
What's going on?

158
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,440
What happened to you?

159
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,159
You homewrecker,
found yourself another man?

160
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,758
Using my boyfriend's money
to keep your little pet,

161
00:10:28,759 --> 00:10:31,280
and now you dare hit my brother!

162
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:47,558
Alright, so we've all got a clear picture of
what happened,

163
00:10:47,559 --> 00:10:49,879
and no one's disputing the facts, right?

164
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:54,518
You, next time, think before you act.
Stay calm.

165
00:10:54,519 --> 00:10:58,199
Don't just barge into someone's home
and cause a scene.

166
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,119
That could be considered affray.

167
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:03,880
You should be grateful
Fu Ming Yu isn't pressing charges.

168
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,239
- Sorry for the trouble.
- No problem. That's my job.

169
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,919
Is there anything else my friend needs to do?

170
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,039
She's all set.

171
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,599
Just go to window three, sign out,
and you're free to go.

172
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,359
- Got it, thanks.
- This way.

173
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,678
Officer, wait. How is this fair?

174
00:11:14,679 --> 00:11:15,919
She broke up a marriage.

175
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:18,079
Why does she get to sign and leave?

176
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,398
Calm down.

177
00:11:19,399 --> 00:11:22,399
As far as I know, you're not even married.
Whose marriage did she break up?

178
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,999
But look what she did to my brother!
He looks like a punching bag!

179
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,918
Why don't you ask your brother who hit him?

180
00:11:26,919 --> 00:11:28,398
If she didn't, then who did? Me?

181
00:11:28,399 --> 00:11:30,719
Yes, it was you!

182
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,079
- No way. When did I ever hit you?
- You did!

183
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:35,439
Alright, that's enough!
Both of you, come with me.

184
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:36,719
Over here.

185
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,399
Come on.

186
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,719
Are you feeling unwell?

187
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,399
No.

188
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:45,079
I skipped breakfast.

189
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,759
Old issue.

190
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,319
You're all set.

191
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,798
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

192
00:11:49,799 --> 00:11:51,360
You're welcome.

193
00:11:54,683 --> 00:11:56,479
What exactly happened this morning?

194
00:11:56,480 --> 00:12:00,679
I guess Yan An gave her the cold shoulder
instead of breaking up cleanly.

195
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,279
She must've been watching for a few days.

196
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,359
Saw him at my place last night

197
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:07,240
and came knocking this morning,
looking for proof.

198
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:12,960
I did warn you to be careful with Yan An.

199
00:12:13,781 --> 00:12:15,631
Mr. Fu.

200
00:12:15,633 --> 00:12:17,513
Thank you.

201
00:12:20,885 --> 00:12:24,144
Didn't expect to hear that from you.

202
00:12:24,146 --> 00:12:27,280
I genuinely mean it.

203
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:30,600
And...

204
00:12:31,705 --> 00:12:36,547
Sorry about last night. I was pretty harsh.

205
00:12:36,549 --> 00:12:39,878
So, on top of everything, I get an apology too?

206
00:12:39,879 --> 00:12:42,160
Do you accept it?

207
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,479
I'll take the thanks.

208
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:47,960
As for the apology, you can keep it.

209
00:12:50,879 --> 00:12:52,840
I'll take this call.

210
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:59,479
- Mr. Yan.
- They didn't hurt you, did they?

211
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,159
What's going on?
You need me to send someone over?

212
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,439
It's already handled.

213
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:08,479
But your ex might be looking at
10 days to two weeks in detention.

214
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,878
She's in there crying and throwing a fit.

215
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:12,199
Maybe you should take some responsibility.

216
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,959
I am so sorry.

217
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,399
This is completely on me.

218
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,279
I'm out of town for work right now,
but I'll be back tomorrow.

219
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:19,159
I'll come and apologize to you in person.

220
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,594
Really, don't bother.

221
00:13:21,596 --> 00:13:25,239
And that gift from last night was way too much.

222
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,918
- I'll return it to you.
- No.

223
00:13:26,919 --> 00:13:28,319
If you'd said no yesterday, fine.

224
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:30,359
But after what happened today,
you have to keep it.

225
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:33,279
- Consider it my apology.
- A verbal apology is enough.

226
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:35,119
And I'm not going to hold it against you.

227
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,678
I'm not that petty.

228
00:13:36,679 --> 00:13:38,199
You don't need to dwell on it.

229
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:42,039
Besides, I'm not really into
that kind of stuff anyway.

230
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:44,120
- Then what are you into?
- Then what are you into?

231
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:57,879
Airplanes.

232
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:02,280
The Z101 domestic airplane.

233
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,360
Let's talk when I'm back in Jiang City.

234
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,959
Ruan! Are you alright?

235
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:14,239
Is everything settled?

236
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,679
Yeah, it's fine. I'll explain at home.

237
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,719
Mr. Fu, thank you for today.

238
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,079
We'll be going now.

239
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,199
- Let me give you a ride.
- It's okay, I drove.

240
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,639
Thanks again, Mr. Fu.

241
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,799
We'll take it from here.

242
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,600
See you, boss.

243
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,559
Well, I'll be damned.

244
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,439
Can't believe I voted for Mr. Yan back then.

245
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:43,239
He's that unreliable.

246
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,719
He's a decent guy, honestly.

247
00:14:45,721 --> 00:14:47,559
But his personal life is a mess.

248
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:51,359
Yeah, guys like that are only good as friends.

249
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,599
They're not boyfriend material.

250
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,981
So what are you going to do about him?

251
00:14:55,983 --> 00:14:57,759
What else?

252
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:01,119
I'll lay it all out and show him the door.

253
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,839
What about Mr. Fu, though?

254
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,399
What's he got to do with anything?

255
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:08,879
This time he really upped his game.

256
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,558
If he hadn't been there,
you'd have been in real danger today.

257
00:15:11,559 --> 00:15:13,839
Yeah, the hero saves the damsel.

258
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,680
There must be something.

259
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:22,479
If he really fell for me,
then that only means one thing.

260
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,518
What?

261
00:15:23,519 --> 00:15:25,148
What?

262
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:29,400
He's got a thing for punishment.

263
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:51,839
I see.

264
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:54,039
Holding out on us?

265
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:56,399
Who's the guy you're texting?

266
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,359
Si Xiao Zhen, come clean.

267
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,479
- No!
- Who is it?

268
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,239
Give me my phone! Let me reply.

269
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,759
- Please!
- Who is it? Spill.

270
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,800
AkaQiu.

271
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,959
Who?

272
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,518
Lu Ming. His name is Lu Ming.

273
00:16:09,519 --> 00:16:12,200
His handle is AkaQiu.

274
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,439
Where'd you meet him?

275
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,280
Give it back!

276
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,799
See.

277
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,359
It's this game.

278
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:24,160
This is me, and this is him.

279
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:27,879
Si Xiao Zhen, you are 26 years old,

280
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:33,398
and you're online
dating some guy called AkaQiu?

281
00:16:33,399 --> 00:16:37,879
And who was it that said,
"men are a distraction"

282
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,839
and that "I'm married to my work?"

283
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,920
You don't get it. This is different.

284
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:47,559
I used to think it was impossible
to find the right match.

285
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,999
When I wasn't doing well,
no one was interested;

286
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,279
when I was doing great,
I felt like I was too good for anyone.

287
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:56,119
So I stayed single.

288
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,559
But this one's different.

289
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,319
I found him when I wasn't even looking.

290
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:03,278
He's someone I never would've met
even when I was at my best.

291
00:17:03,279 --> 00:17:09,279
And you know, the older you get,
the lower the odds of that spark.

292
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:13,439
Alright, that's enough.

293
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,439
We're just worried you're getting scammed.

294
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,119
What's there to scam?

295
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,519
I'm still paying off my car loan.

296
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:19,558
- Exactly.
- True.

297
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:21,920
I forgot about that.

298
00:17:22,759 --> 00:17:24,714
About time.

299
00:17:24,716 --> 00:17:27,399
Ladies, time to clock in.

300
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,359
- Let me go change.
- Okay.

301
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:31,960
We'll grill you more at the lounge.

302
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,479
Hello, Mr. Fu.

303
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,080
Mr. Fu.

304
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,919
They're going to my lounge with me.

305
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:58,119
Your stomach's off,
but you're going to a lounge?

306
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:01,400
Since when does going to a bar mean
I have to drink?

307
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,239
I'll go get the car.

308
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:08,479
Meet you out front.

309
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:11,160
Goodbye, boss.

310
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,800
What are you doing here?

311
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:26,079
Came to drop off some medicine.

312
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:27,919
I'm feeling much better.

313
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:31,054
Just finished the congee you sent.

314
00:18:31,056 --> 00:18:33,439
There's a pill case inside.

315
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:36,000
You can keep some stomach medicine on you.

316
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,479
Thank you.

317
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,879
Well...

318
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,720
I should go.

319
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,160
No drinking.

320
00:19:21,950 --> 00:19:23,920
I'm taking the elevator too.

321
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,999
Up?

322
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,520
Down.

323
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,640
I'm heading to B1.

324
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,679
Alright. See you.

325
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:08,320
Bye.

326
00:20:16,253 --> 00:20:17,813
Going out?

327
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,520
Mr. Fu, you're back.

328
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:13,519
Here's your dessert.

329
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:15,759
Why is it that when we grow up,

330
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:18,559
we get so shy about sharing our love lives
with our besties?

331
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:21,439
I remember back in the day,
if I made eye contact with a guy,

332
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:24,040
I'd run straight to my friends
and spill everything.

333
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:33,200
Maybe because it's uncertain.

334
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:38,199
You don't know
if something that's just started will work.

335
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:42,599
And even if it does,
you don't know how long it'll last.

336
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:46,319
So if it's all going to end in nothing anyway,

337
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:51,799
maybe it's better to keep it to yourself,
like it never happened.

338
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:53,759
That's ridiculous.

339
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:57,559
Every relationship leaves its mark,
whether they like it or not.

340
00:21:57,560 --> 00:22:00,920
Why hide their heads in the sand
like an ostrich?

341
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:03,679
I think you're right.

342
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:06,320
That's why I never hide anything.

343
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:16,640
Don't look at me like that.

344
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:24,119
I only go for strangers.

345
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,758
Thank you.

346
00:22:25,759 --> 00:22:28,160
Excuse me, your red wine.

347
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,199
You ran over my foot.

348
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:10,119
- Ruan Si Xian, what's the rush?
- It's okay.

349
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:12,559
Manager Wang,
there're few simulators available.

350
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,039
I need to grab one before they're all taken.

351
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:18,319
Mr. Fu, I...

352
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:20,639
There's a second shoot tomorrow afternoon.

353
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,039
Don't stay up too late.

354
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:25,160
- Make sure you're in good shape.
- Another shoot?

355
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,839
Fine, I'll do it.

356
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:30,279
Cooperating with the shoot is part of my duty.

357
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:34,039
But personally, I think an airline
should be about operations first.

358
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:35,379
If the campaign focused more on

359
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:37,838
showing passengers
what we're actually capable of,

360
00:23:37,839 --> 00:23:39,840
that'd probably work better.

361
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:48,040
Anyway, I'll be going now.

362
00:23:58,973 --> 00:24:00,693
Are you alright?

363
00:24:05,122 --> 00:24:07,359
Dear passenger,
we have arrived at your destination.

364
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:09,880
Please exit from the right side.

365
00:24:11,437 --> 00:24:13,919
What, you don't want to get out?

366
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:17,672
What do you think
if I open a studio in Jiang City?

367
00:24:17,674 --> 00:24:18,793
Go for it.

368
00:24:18,795 --> 00:24:21,559
Need any help? I'll handle it.

369
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:23,999
Are you that reliable?

370
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,919
I'm nothing like Fu Ming Yu.

371
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,839
Reliability is my middle name.

372
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:29,999
Alright then. Find me a space.

373
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,599
Go ahead. What are your requirements?

374
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:35,599
I need room for an office,
a place for client meetings,

375
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:38,119
and a separate area I can use as a studio.

376
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:41,119
So you need a big space.

377
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:43,239
Give me three days.
I'll give you a few options.

378
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,919
Deal.

379
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:47,280
- I'm off.
- Bye.

380
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:52,640
Sister Zheng.

381
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,479
What?

382
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:58,359
Do me a favor, too.

383
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:02,000
Are you playing the exchange game with me?

384
00:25:03,533 --> 00:25:06,013
I'm really out of options.

385
00:25:08,039 --> 00:25:10,000
You're the only one I can turn to.

386
00:25:14,449 --> 00:25:16,078
Spill.

387
00:25:16,079 --> 00:25:19,399
Help me get Ruan Si Xian to meet up with me.

388
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:21,268
You've taken photos of her before.

389
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:22,759
You've got a way in, right?

390
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:24,719
Meet up?

391
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,599
You brat. What are you plotting?

392
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:29,559
I'm going to confess
to your future sister-in-law.

393
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:30,959
I've been chasing her for a while.

394
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:34,448
If I don't make a move now,
I'm letting her down.

395
00:25:34,450 --> 00:25:39,359
Hold on, so you call me "sister,"
and I'm supposed to call her "sister-in-law"?

396
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:41,879
You've been chasing her for ages
and can't even get her out,

397
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,399
and you want to confess?

398
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:47,119
- Where do you get that confidence, kid?
- Don't worry about that, Ms. Zheng.

399
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:50,319
- Please, help me this once.
- No.

400
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:51,518
Just this once.

401
00:25:51,519 --> 00:25:53,159
It's not like I ask you all the time.

402
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:54,759
I can't. It's wrong.

403
00:25:54,760 --> 00:25:56,399
Zheng You An, you're so cold.

404
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:57,999
I even called you "sister."

405
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,839
I have principles.

406
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:02,039
You're just stringing her along.

407
00:26:02,040 --> 00:26:04,199
You know exactly what you're like, don't you?

408
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,639
No, I don't.

409
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,879
Anyway, take this as a lesson.

410
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:10,719
Your ex-girlfriend showed up at her place
making a scene.

411
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:13,159
It's a mercy
she didn't even call the police on you.

412
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,278
And you're still not done?

413
00:26:14,279 --> 00:26:17,919
But I need a chance to apologize.

414
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:20,599
Every time I bring it up, she says she's busy.

415
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:22,719
She probably doesn't even want your apology.

416
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:25,919
She just wants you to stay away.

417
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:29,278
Please, Ms. Zheng, just this once.

418
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:31,358
I'll get you a year's membership
at the climbing gym.

419
00:26:31,359 --> 00:26:32,838
You think I need your membership?

420
00:26:32,839 --> 00:26:34,719
Lifetime.

421
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:36,480
I don't need it.

422
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:40,919
Your studio space, your staff, your clients.
All of it.

423
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,880
I'll take care of everything.

424
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:50,240
I'll think about it.

425
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:53,279
Hey, thanks!

426
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:55,239
Before I agreed, I was "Ms. Zheng."
Now I'm "hey?"

427
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,439
You looking for a smack?

428
00:26:56,440 --> 00:26:58,120
Bye.

429
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:21,080
I knew it was bad,
but I didn't know it was that bad.

430
00:27:21,839 --> 00:27:24,439
Hello, Uncle Qin, Uncle Liu.

431
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:25,879
Where's Mom, Dad?

432
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:28,759
Went to scout locations for her art exhibition
with your Uncle Guo.

433
00:27:28,760 --> 00:27:30,680
She'll be back soon.

434
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:47,719
Seven out of 10 hotels in Europe
are losing money.

435
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:51,039
What's the point of staying
in the European market?

436
00:27:51,040 --> 00:27:54,679
Shut down the seven in Europe
and the three in Australia.

437
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:58,199
Use the capital we save
to double down on the domestic market.

438
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:01,879
But Mr. Zheng, if we do that, our brand's--

439
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,799
The global economy is slowing down.

440
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:07,459
It's time to tighten our belts.

441
00:28:07,460 --> 00:28:11,820
We need to drop the illusions, be realistic,

442
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:16,000
and face the facts.

443
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:41,999
Cabin door is open now. Rapid decompression.

444
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,480
Cabin decompression. Emergency descent.

445
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,559
Establish communication.

446
00:28:52,560 --> 00:28:53,838
How do you read me?

447
00:28:53,839 --> 00:28:55,239
I read you five.

448
00:28:55,240 --> 00:28:56,439
I read you five, too.

449
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:59,400
Check cabin altitude.
Vertical speed unmanageable.

450
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:01,519
Thrust idle, open descent.

451
00:29:01,520 --> 00:29:04,319
Altitude backup. Altitude 17,000 feet, blue.

452
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:05,439
Confirmed.

453
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:08,519
Our current position, grid altitude 3,900.

454
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:10,439
Confirmed.

455
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:12,799
3,900, 128 set.

456
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:14,600
Confirmed.

457
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,999
3,900, 128, blue.

458
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,639
- Check.
- Fuselage damage.

459
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:20,799
Maintain current speed.

460
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:22,598
Emergency descent! Emergency descent!

461
00:29:22,599 --> 00:29:23,599
Mayday! Mayday! Mayday!

462
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:27,520
Hengshi Air 5101,
cabin decompression, emergency descent.

463
00:29:37,119 --> 00:29:38,880
100,

464
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,399
50,

465
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:43,518
40,

466
00:29:43,519 --> 00:29:44,598
30,

467
00:29:44,599 --> 00:29:46,099
20,

468
00:29:48,319 --> 00:29:50,160
throttle back.

469
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:22,554
Okay.

470
00:30:22,556 --> 00:30:24,519
Alright, that's it for today.

471
00:30:24,520 --> 00:30:26,880
Instructor, I'm off.

472
00:30:32,243 --> 00:30:35,159
You've been getting better
since the inaugural flight.

473
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:37,358
You're sharp, mentor.

474
00:30:37,359 --> 00:30:39,719
The inaugural flight really hit me.

475
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:42,079
I know there's still a lot to learn,

476
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:46,440
but I can't wait
to get back in the captain's seat.

477
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:50,159
Don't put all your energy into work.

478
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:53,739
You need to make progress
in your personal life too.

479
00:30:53,741 --> 00:30:55,239
My personal life is fine.

480
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:57,519
What else is there to improve?

481
00:30:57,520 --> 00:31:01,680
I've noticed Mr. Fu seems to
take good care of you.

482
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:04,799
He does? Who told you that?

483
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:06,879
Fine, I won't ask.

484
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:09,399
How are you getting home? Need a ride?

485
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,759
No, I want to stay a little longer.

486
00:31:11,760 --> 00:31:13,680
Run another session.

487
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:19,319
It's almost dawn.

488
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,033
Get some rest.

489
00:31:21,035 --> 00:31:23,240
I will, mentor.

490
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,080
Mr. Fu.

491
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:51,640
Up all night?

492
00:31:52,800 --> 00:31:54,039
Get in.

493
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:56,238
I'll take you back.

494
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,384
No, thank you.

495
00:31:57,386 --> 00:31:59,386
I've called a car.

496
00:32:01,415 --> 00:32:03,439
[Cancel the trip]

497
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:04,599
Get in.

498
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:08,560
The sooner you're home,
the sooner you can rest.

499
00:32:20,266 --> 00:32:21,986
Thanks.

500
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,559
You practiced all night.

501
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:52,079
Must be tired.

502
00:32:52,080 --> 00:32:53,394
Don't worry, Mr. Fu.

503
00:32:53,396 --> 00:32:55,119
I've never needed much sleep.

504
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:56,919
And it's not like I'm flying a real mission.

505
00:32:56,920 --> 00:33:00,200
I can handle the shoot today.

506
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:06,279
We can postpone the shoot.

507
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:09,320
Just go home and get some good rest.

508
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:13,400
I'm sorry.

509
00:33:14,434 --> 00:33:18,039
I didn't realize this shoot was that important.

510
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:19,720
It's not.

511
00:33:24,880 --> 00:33:28,400
The campaign plan isn't finalized yet.

512
00:33:30,110 --> 00:33:33,840
You're not changing it back to
a solo shoot, are you?

513
00:33:35,057 --> 00:33:38,919
Do you think I change my mind that easily?

514
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,920
Who knows?

515
00:33:47,130 --> 00:33:49,854
Zhang, pull over up ahead.

516
00:33:49,856 --> 00:33:53,919
Mr. Fu, you're not going to
throw me out, are you?

517
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:55,278
I've been sitting too long.

518
00:33:55,279 --> 00:33:57,520
Let's get out and stretch.

519
00:34:41,119 --> 00:34:42,999
Fine.

520
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:44,984
Typical boss move.

521
00:34:44,986 --> 00:34:48,400
But I get paid, so I get it.

522
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:31,999
Didn't expect you
to have such a romantic streak, Mr. Fu.

523
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:34,079
Just happened to see it.

524
00:35:34,080 --> 00:35:36,200
Figured it was worth sharing.

525
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:41,399
I thought you'd be mad
I stayed up all night practicing

526
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:43,200
and messing up the shoot.

527
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,479
She started from the bottom,

528
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:49,119
but she was the first to take the exam
and get her license.

529
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:52,200
We can only imagine
what she put in to get there.

530
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:55,279
Don't worry about that.

531
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:58,159
First and foremost,
you're a pilot at Hengshi Air.

532
00:35:58,160 --> 00:36:01,999
Practicing late to hone your skills
is perfectly understandable.

533
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:07,279
I'll remind the publicity team
to schedule around your work hours.

534
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,159
So the shoot today...

535
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:12,638
Like I said, postponed.

536
00:36:12,639 --> 00:36:15,680
You go home and rest.

537
00:36:19,240 --> 00:36:20,999
Of course,

538
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:24,400
you can enjoy the sunrise for a little while.
It's beautiful.

539
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:52,400
What's wrong?

540
00:36:55,039 --> 00:36:58,118
Nothing. I'm just too sleepy.

541
00:36:58,119 --> 00:37:00,440
I should get home and sleep.

542
00:37:31,044 --> 00:37:33,759
Hello? Is it time for the shoot?

543
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,118
Are you Hengshi people all about work?

544
00:37:36,119 --> 00:37:37,319
Don't you have a life?

545
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:38,959
Then what's this call about?

546
00:37:38,960 --> 00:37:43,718
I had a great time last time,
but we never really got to know each other.

547
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:47,480
I wanted to see if you're free today.
Grab a meal?

548
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:50,799
Is something going on?

549
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:51,879
Don't be so tense.

550
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:53,301
It's just dinner.

551
00:37:53,303 --> 00:37:55,399
I'll send you the restaurant location, okay?

552
00:37:55,400 --> 00:37:58,080
Be there or be square. Be there or be square!

553
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:01,399
You're amazing, Sister Zheng.

554
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:03,519
Swooped in before she even noticed.

555
00:38:03,520 --> 00:38:04,919
Don't get too full of yourself.

556
00:38:04,920 --> 00:38:06,279
This is just a trade.

557
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:08,920
Didn't you say you'd take me to see the studio?

558
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:13,880
Come on.

559
00:38:15,239 --> 00:38:16,399
It's right upstairs.

560
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,558
A 500-square-meter space.

561
00:38:17,559 --> 00:38:19,121
All yours.

562
00:38:19,123 --> 00:38:21,518
I don't need that much space.

563
00:38:21,519 --> 00:38:23,119
No harm in checking it out.

564
00:38:23,120 --> 00:38:24,920
See how it feels.

565
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:37,959
Hello, do you have a reservation?

566
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,079
Private Room 520.

567
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:40,720
This way, please.

568
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:01,199
Wasn't Zheng You An supposed to meet me here?

569
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:03,120
What are you doing here?

570
00:39:04,786 --> 00:39:06,506
Have a seat.

571
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:11,960
I thought it was just going to be me
and Zheng You An.

572
00:39:13,490 --> 00:39:18,680
To be honest,
I asked You An to help set this up.

573
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:22,519
Are you serious?

574
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:24,542
Last time you were the one who paid.

575
00:39:24,544 --> 00:39:27,198
I never found the right time
to return the favor.

576
00:39:27,199 --> 00:39:32,399
And with all that awkwardness before,

577
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:35,537
I didn't have a choice. I had to pull this.

578
00:39:35,539 --> 00:39:38,879
Mr. Yan, we're friends after all.

579
00:39:38,880 --> 00:39:40,198
Do we have to keep score like this?

580
00:39:40,199 --> 00:39:41,678
I'm not trying to keep score.

581
00:39:41,679 --> 00:39:46,319
I just wanted to buy you a simple meal.

582
00:39:46,320 --> 00:39:48,680
Does this look simple to you?

583
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:52,319
And Mr. Yan, I have exams coming up.

584
00:39:52,320 --> 00:39:53,559
I'm really busy.

585
00:39:53,560 --> 00:39:57,119
Let's do dinner another time.

586
00:39:57,120 --> 00:39:58,744
Ruan Si Xian.

587
00:39:58,746 --> 00:40:00,666
Ruan Si Xian.

588
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:06,118
If I could clear up all that mess from before,
would I still have a chance?

589
00:40:06,119 --> 00:40:09,399
Mr. Yan, we're fine just being friends.

590
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:11,518
- Ruan Si Xian, just let me--
- There's nothing to say.

591
00:40:11,519 --> 00:40:15,480
Unless you don't even want to
be my friend anymore.

592
00:40:50,719 --> 00:40:53,320
- Mr. Fu.
- What's up?

593
00:40:58,840 --> 00:41:00,644
Just...

594
00:41:00,646 --> 00:41:02,646
Just saying hi.

595
00:41:03,779 --> 00:41:06,579
Actually, there's something
I've been wondering about.

596
00:41:09,540 --> 00:41:14,420
Since you like Bo'ao Air so much,
why did you come here?

597
00:41:21,939 --> 00:41:27,680
Mr. Fu, you're the one
who begged me to come, remember?

598
00:41:29,102 --> 00:41:31,999
If you wanted double the signing bonus,

599
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,558
Yan An would've given it to you too,
wouldn't he?

600
00:41:34,559 --> 00:41:35,679
He would.

601
00:41:35,680 --> 00:41:38,360
He'd give me four times if I asked.

602
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:44,919
Are you worried
I'm secretly favoring Bo'ao Air?

603
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:47,320
You're still avoiding my question.

604
00:41:57,806 --> 00:42:00,166
Why did you come to Hengshi Air?

605
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,840
For me?

606
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:17,239
Is your nose a runway
or are your eyes swimming pools?

607
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:19,559
Are your eyelashes brushes,
or are your abs a trampoline?

608
00:42:19,560 --> 00:42:22,679
Do you seriously think you're so hot
that you'd make people save the world?

609
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:23,799
If you're so great, why settle for CEO?

610
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:25,720
Why don't you fly yourself to Mars?

611
00:42:36,080 --> 00:42:37,880
For me?

612
00:42:43,066 --> 00:42:48,119
Mr. Fu, are you feeling a little tired lately?

613
00:42:48,120 --> 00:42:51,240
Maybe you should go get some rest?

614
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:56,319
Don't forget there's a shoot tomorrow.

615
00:42:56,320 --> 00:42:57,919
Got it.

616
00:42:57,920 --> 00:43:01,079
I won't drop the ball when it comes to work.

617
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:04,600
I'll be off then.

618
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:08,919
Is your nose a runway
or are your eyes swimming pools?

619
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,319
Are your abs a trampoline?

620
00:43:10,320 --> 00:43:12,480
Why don't you go fly yourself to Mars?

621
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:29,119
Ruan, the photography team is set and ready.

622
00:43:29,120 --> 00:43:31,519
We won't cut into your training time too much.

623
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:32,959
Come on.

624
00:43:32,960 --> 00:43:34,719
One more thing.

625
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:39,559
Fu Ming Yu made sure the shooting plan
fits your schedule and your preferences.

626
00:43:39,560 --> 00:43:41,679
So, ready for the shoot?

627
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:43,240
Ready.
